# Design workflow auto-scan

Agents must load design context automatically. The user should not need to paste preamble prompts.

## Session start (every conversation)

Before responding to the first user message or taking action:

1. Read `DESIGN_WORKFLOW.md`
2. Read `.cursor/design-memory/approved-direction.md` and note **Approval status**
3. Skim `.cursor/design-memory/creative-thesis.md` and `.cursor/experience-memory/critical-user-journeys.md` for `[UNRESOLVED]` fields
4. Determine **current phase** (table below)
5. Check SEO foundation (see `seo-ai-visibility.mdc` Auto-implementation table). Note what is missing.
6. State internally (brief, not verbose to user unless relevant): current phase, approval status, next required skill, SEO gaps

Do not wait for the user to ask you to read these files or implement SEO.

## Full scan (design-related work)

Before any task touching visual design, layout, typography, motion, marketing pages, app UI, customer-facing copy, design tokens, CSS/theme, or brand assets:

Read in full:

- `DESIGN_WORKFLOW.md`
- `.cursor/rules/fajita-master-directive.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/design-principles.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/anti-ai-slop.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/brand-constraints.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/frontend-quality.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/seo-ai-visibility.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/pixel-perfect-quality.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/experience-quality.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/state-completeness.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/perceived-performance.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/trust-and-claims.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/release-quality-gates.mdc`
- `.cursor/design-memory/creative-thesis.md`
- `.cursor/design-memory/approved-direction.md`
- `.cursor/design-memory/rejected-patterns.md`
- `.cursor/design-memory/visual-decisions.md`
- `.cursor/design-memory/critique-log.md` (if it has entries)
- `.cursor/experience-memory/experience-principles.md`
- `.cursor/experience-memory/critical-user-journeys.md`
- `.cursor/experience-memory/interface-state-inventory.md`
- `.cursor/experience-memory/release-scorecard.md`

Then invoke the skill for the current phase (see table). Follow that skill's workflow before writing UI code.

## Light scan (non-design work)

For backend, infra, database, scripts, config, or docs that do not change customer-facing surfaces:

- Read `approved-direction.md` status only
- Do not invoke creative skills
- If the task later touches UI files or public routes, upgrade to full scan first

## SEO scan (public routes and metadata)

Before creating or changing any indexable route, metadata, `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, or `llms.txt`:

- Read `.cursor/rules/seo-ai-visibility.mdc` in full
- Apply per-page and launch checklists before merge

## Experience scan (product behavior work)

Before onboarding, auth, billing, app shell, workflows, states, analytics, demos, or release:

- Read experience rules and relevant `experience-memory/` files in full
- Invoke matching Experience Phase skill (A–G) from `DESIGN_WORKFLOW.md`
- Update `interface-state-inventory.md` before marking features complete
- Update `release-scorecard.md` before calling release ready

## Phase detection

Infer phase from repository state and design memory. When unclear, default to the earliest incomplete phase.

| Phase | Condition | Auto-invoke skill |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | `creative-thesis.md` has major `[UNRESOLVED]` fields | Inspect repo; update thesis. No UI. |
| 2 | `approved-direction.md` status is "Not yet approved" | `creative-director` |
| 3 | Direction approved or recommended but brand world incomplete | `brand-world-builder`, `brand-copy-director`, `typography-director` |
| 4 | Brand world documented but no visual slice in codebase | `editorial-layout`, `signature-moment-designer`, `motion-choreographer` |
| 5 | Visual slice exists but `critique-log.md` shows no passing QA | `visual-qa-critic` |
| 6 | Slice QA passed; tokens not encoded | `design-system-engineer` |
| 7 | Tokens exist; marketing routes incomplete | `editorial-layout`, `conversion-experience-designer` |
| 8 | Marketing done; app UI not art-directed | `product-ui-art-director` |
| 9 | App exists; responsive QA incomplete | `responsive-art-director` |
| 10 | Implementation done; final scores below 9 | `visual-qa-critic` |
| 11 | Visual QA passed; production hardening pending | `frontend-quality.mdc` + `seo-ai-visibility.mdc` + `layout-perfection-critic` + Experience Phase G |

### Experience phases (parallel track)

| Phase | Condition | Auto-invoke |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A | `critical-user-journeys.md` mostly unresolved | `product-experience-director` |
| B | No interactive demo | `interactive-demo-engineer`, `content-realism-editor` |
| C | No onboarding/activation path | `onboarding-activation-architect` |
| D | P0 states Pending in inventory | `interface-state-director`, `microinteraction-director` |
| E | Trust register gaps or perf unmeasured | `trust-experience-designer`, `perceived-performance-engineer` |
| F | Analytics not wired to UI | `product-analytics-architect` |
| G | Release scorecard not pass | `cross-browser-qa-engineer`, `maintainability-critic`, `visual-qa-critic` |

User instructions override phase detection when they explicitly name a phase or scope.

## Implementation gates (enforce automatically)

| Gate | Block until |
| --- | --- |
| Broad UI build | `approved-direction.md` is **Approved** (not merely recommended) |
| Full marketing site | Phase 5 visual slice QA passed |
| Design system tokens | Phase 5 passed; direction approved |
| Full app UI | Phase 6 tokens encoded |
| Ship / PR for design | Phase 10 scores ≥ 9 or documented exception in `critique-log.md` |
| Public page or marketing work | SEO foundation exists (`robots`, `sitemap`, `llms.txt`, `metadataBase`, root JSON-LD). If missing, **implement automatically** before or with the page. |
| Any new public route | Per-route metadata, sitemap entry, and index intent in same change |
| Vertical slice scale-out | Vertical slice passed creative + experience review (`DESIGN_WORKFLOW.md`) |
| Release / ship | `release-scorecard.md` all blocking items Pass or documented exception |
| Feature complete | P0 states Done in `interface-state-inventory.md` |

If a gate blocks the user's request, say which gate failed and which skill to run. Offer to run it. **Exception:** SEO foundation gaps should be fixed by the agent immediately, not blocked waiting for user permission.

## After design work (automatic)

Without being asked:

- Update relevant design-memory files per the active skill
- Run screenshot QA at required breakpoints when UI changed
- Log findings in `critique-log.md`
- Apply per-page SEO checklist from `seo-ai-visibility.mdc` when public routes changed
- Run `layout-perfection-critic` when CSS, layout, or markdown changed
- Update `experience-memory/` when journeys, states, interactions, trust, perf, or analytics change
- Run relevant Experience Phase skill when product behavior changes

## What the user does not need to paste

Never require the user to provide:

- "Read DESIGN_WORKFLOW.md"
- "Read design-memory"
- "Invoke creative-director"

This rule replaces those preambles. The user can jump straight to intent: "build the homepage," "run phase 4," "fix the hero on mobile."

